# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": any line may use any name the block binds, and the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), ch. 8 (a clause is chosen by its pattern; a widget application is transparent, its plain result a value) and ruling TC: loud gives 7, so `w` is 14, the clause `k` builds "one 14" and "two 14" at 0 and 1, `@Twice` its label at 2, the arm its own at 3; soft gives 20, so `w` is 40, and builds nothing in its arm. Never run: prismc refuses the program.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 14")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 14")
    2: Ui.Label(text="twice 7")
    3: Ui.Label(text="seven")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="one 40")
    1: Ui.Label(text="two 40")
    2: Ui.Label(text="twice 20")
